\title{Polynomial constraints and evaluation filtrations}
\taxon{Definition}
\tag{definition}
\meta{defines}{constrained polynomial space; evaluation space; dimension increment; evaluation-filtration increment}
\meta{dependencies}{[Univariate polynomial maps](cn-0064); [Interpolation nodes](cn-0063)}
\meta{provenance}{[OpenAI, 23 September 2026](cn-0042), proof of Lemma 2.1; reconstructed as a reading account on 9 October 2026. [Lean source: PolynomialFiltration](/source-material/openai-math/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/Crossing/PolynomialFiltration.lean).}

\p{Let #{W} be a finite-dimensional real vector space, the ambient space of polynomial values, and let #{U_1,\ldots,U_m\subseteq W} be subspaces. Choose distinct real [interpolation nodes](cn-0063) #{t_1,\ldots,t_m}, at which we impose conditions on those vector values. For a subspace #{Z\subseteq W}, write #{Z[\xi]} for the [univariate polynomial maps](cn-0064) with coefficients in #{Z}: #{P(\xi)=\sum_{r=0}^{h}z_r\xi^r} with each #{z_r\in Z}.}

\p{The \em{constrained polynomial space}, for #{h\geq0}, is}

##{\mathcal P_h(Z)=\{P\in Z[\xi]:\deg P\leq h,\ P(t_i)\in U_i\text{ for every }i\},\qquad \mathcal P_{-1}(Z)=0.}

\p{Each constraint means #{\sum_{r=0}^{h}t_i^r z_r\in U_i}. This sum already belongs to #{Z}, so the permitted value lies in #{U_i\cap Z}. The coefficients form a tuple in #{Z^{h+1}}, and these are linear conditions on that tuple.}

\p{Its \em{evaluation space} and \em{dimension increment} are}

##{E_h(Z;t)=\{P(t):P\in\mathcal P_h(Z)\},\qquad k_h(Z)=\dim\mathcal P_h(Z)-\dim\mathcal P_{h-1}(Z),\quad k_{-1}(Z)=0.}

\p{For a fixed #{t_*\notin\{t_1,\ldots,t_m\}}, called a [non-node](cn-0063), the spaces #{E_h(W;t_*)} are nested. After [identifying their dimensions](cn-0020), write #{\ell_h=k_h(W)-k_{h-1}(W)} for the \em{evaluation-filtration increment}. Nonnegativity of these increments is a consequence of nesting.}

\p{Lean uses a strict degree bound: its space indexed by #{h+1} corresponds to the paper's #{\mathcal P_h}. The [Lean guide](cn-0038) records this shift.}
